                <pb facs="1036" n="878" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg878"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Furniss to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                                Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-05-22"><hi rendition="#italic">May 22,
                        1906</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 61.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to report that President Nord Alexis
                    yesterday nominated Mr. Pauléus Sannon secretary of foreign relations, vice Mr.
                    Murville Férère, resigned.</p>
                <p>Mr. Sannon was born April 7, 1870, at Aux Cayes. He was educated in Haiti and
                    Paris, having spent seven years at the latter place.</p>
                <p>He is said to be an author of importance, his principal works being Haiti et le
                    Régime Parlementaire, 1898; Boisrond-Tonnerre et son Temps, 1904; Essai
                    Historique sur la Révolution de 1843, 1905.</p>
                <p>The only public offices held by him have been chief of bureau of Aux Cayes
                    custom-house from 1900 to 1905, and from that date until his nomination as
                    secretary of foreign relations he was head official of the department of finance
                    of the Jacmel district.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. W. Furniss.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
